---
/**
 * P6 Universities: /partner-with-us/universities/ (T3, implements doc 04 matrix 4.5).
 * C1 to C14 in order, as the numbered table in doc 06 P6, without C3 (Cost of Waiting) and C4 (Imagine), which the audience pages leave to Home since WP47.
 * WP30c (owner direction 2026-10-14, "less is more"): every CMF band stays, each states its point once. Gone: the In Short summary, the fit check, the
 * standard-inclusions list, the restated scorecard paragraph and the fifth next step.
 * WP36 (cycle-13 reviews): the three pains are statements; the cost question has the one-line route answer and a link to the hub FAQ; the options band carries Home's line that program sizes are not a commitment
 * (a first campus program is read beside "1,000–2,500 trainees" otherwise).
 * WP38 (cycle-15 review): the full evidence band (offered-place and attender income, survey chart, education profile) is a light strip, "Evidence from Our Wider Youth Programs": the trial result, the survey's degree share and
 * employment readings, and the two evidence links. The National University band's heading names the partnership, and its clarifying sentence stays under it.
 * WP39 (cycle-16 review): "What Your Students Get" is three short cards (IncludesBand), not the concern / inclusion / benefit matrix; the Guide band no longer repeats the National University partnership sentence
 * ("The National University Partnership" states it).
 * WP43 (cycle-20 review): the light evidence strip WP38 made ("Evidence from Our Wider Youth Programs": the trial line, the survey line and two links) is gone, because the first band already ends in the linked strip
 * "Broader Evidence from Our Youth Programs" (the trial, the survey, the case studies) and the later strip said it again; the page has no #proof-band now (no page linked it). The survey's degree share stayed in the meta description until WP54.
 * WP47 (owner decision 2026-10-15): the page opens with its own proof and goes straight to its offer. The Cost of Waiting band ("No Placement Evidence Weakens Your Employment Story") and the Imagine band ("What Your Students
 * Leave With") are gone; Home carries them. Nothing on this page depended on them: the certification terms (eligibility, attempts and terms agreed in the program scope), the campus labs as
 * blended-learning centers and the follow-up surveys are stated in the delivery model and in "What Your Students Get". The "Degree Holders Struggle to Find Work" card says "A degree alone does not guarantee a job offer."
 * WP49 (cycle-24 reviews): the institution's pain says what it needs ("Your institution needs placement data it can report to a board or ministry."); "Choose Where to Start" no longer repeats the cost answer's pricing sentence in its lead (the
 * "What Does It Cost?" answer states it; the lead is the program-sizes note); the risk band's eyebrow is "Managed Rollout"; the steps band is "What Happens Next".
 * WP50 (cycle-25 review): the track-record band opens with its origin line ("Since 2014, ..."): the empathy line that restated the problem ("You see capable students finish their degrees and still struggle to find work, and you are asked for
 * placement results you cannot yet show.") is gone from it, because the problem band above says it. EMPATHY.universities stays in copy.ts for JobReady@Campus, where the sentence is its problem band's lead.
 * WP51 (cycle-26 review): the institution's pain is headed "Build Placement Results You Can Publish" (it presumed a deficiency); the closing line under "What Happens Next" ("University partners include National University, the University for Peace
 * (UPEACE) and The City College of New York (CCNY).") is gone, because the three universities are already named above it: "The National University Partnership" band lists them in its University Partners tile (PA-05), and the Track Record band's logo strip (#guide) carries them as logo alt text.
 * WP57 (cycle-29 review, Grok R5): "Choose Where to Start" has no size cards. Its recommended card read as a 1,000–2,500 country-pilot size for a campus program; the band is now its heading and one line, "Start with one campus: cohort size, tracks
 * and labs are set in the discovery session.", and the page keeps its own one primary button (hero, call to action and sticky bar). The program-sizes note that qualified the cards (PROGRAM_SIZES_NOTE) is not on this page any more.
 * WP128 (Opus High run 3, kit 95): "The National University Partnership" says its disclaimer once, in the lead; the first card leaves out the bracketed copy of it, and the second and third cards do not open with their own label.
 * WP136 (Opus High run 11, Polish): "The National University Partnership" has two cards, not three: the University Partners card (PA-05) is gone, because the band is headed for one partner and the three universities are named in the Track Record band's logo alt text; its lead reads "These cards describe ...".
 * WP66 (owner request 2026-10-20): the Track Record band has one proof line, the signed-agreement sentence for universities and colleges (SC-11b, `signed` on PartnerGuideBand: "CodersTrust has signed MOUs, agreements or contracts with ... universities and colleges."); the band's heading says "Since 2014", so the sentence leaves the year to it.
 * WP175 (owner decisions of 28 November 2026: every conversion page follows CMF v3, C1 to C14, in order and coverage; tests/wp175-universities.spec.ts): every band sits in a Tone wrapper (data-cmf). The
 * "See the Program" link moves under the definition, so GEO directly follows the hero. C2–C4 is a declared compression: the PX-02 and PX-05 tiles are pains P1 and P2 (as doc 04 4.5 records), "Placement Results
 * Are Hard to Publish" is P3, and the band ends with the C3 transition line (C3_TRANSITION). C5 opens with the empathy line again (EMPATHY.universities, a fresh line: not the one WP50 retired) and ends with the
 * TalentLEAP method line (METHOD, Q2 (a)); C6 no longer prints the line or its link (WP166-B R3-29 had moved them there), so the method is said once. C6 is the light mechanism band (HomeMechanism, airy), because
 * the C7 trial band (ProofBand, Klein) now follows it and two dark bands never touch (tests/wp47.spec.ts). C7 is the trial band, led by the one-line trial lead (TRIAL_LEAD), then the National University band (it opened
 * the page before the problem band, WP24a) with its links to the broader evidence, then Maria Dewan's story (also moved from before C2). C8 is CAMPUS_INCLUDES (P1 to P3), one gain creator ("Capacity Designed to
 * Stay on Campus", JobReady@Campus's own vignette, PD-06) and "How It Works in Three Steps" (CAMPUS_STEPS). C10 is the short "What Makes CodersTrust Different" band (USPs 3 and 4, doc 04 4.5). C11 "Start with One
 * Campus" returns as its heading and one line (dee46ac1^; WP135 had folded the line into the pilot band, whose first point reads "Start with a first campus program and see its results." again).
 */
import DueDiligenceView from '../../../components/pages/hub/DueDiligenceView.astro';
import LearnerVoice from '../../../components/pages/impact/LearnerVoice.astro';
import LandingLayout from '../../../layouts/LandingLayout.astro';
import HeroBand from '../../../components/sections/HeroBand.astro';
import DefinitionBand from '../../../components/sections/DefinitionBand.astro';
import ProblemBand from '../../../components/sections/ProblemBand.astro';
import IncludesBand from '../../../components/sections/IncludesBand.astro';
import FAQBand from '../../../components/sections/FAQBand.astro';
import RiskReversalBand from '../../../components/sections/RiskReversalBand.astro';
import ProofBand from '../../../components/sections/ProofBand.astro';
import DifferenceBand from '../../../components/sections/DifferenceBand.astro';
import CTABand from '../../../components/ui/CTABand.astro';
import HomeMechanism from '../../../components/pages/home/HomeMechanism.astro';
import Tone from '../../../components/pages/home/Tone.astro';
import PairedEvidence from '../../../components/pages/partners/PairedEvidence.astro';
import GainsPains from '../../../components/pages/partners/GainsPains.astro';
import HowItWorks from '../../../components/pages/partners/HowItWorks.astro';
import OfferCards from '../../../components/pages/partners/OfferCards.astro';
import PartnerGuideBand from '../../../components/pages/partners/PartnerGuideBand.astro';
import RouteLink from '../../../components/pages/partners/RouteLink.astro';
import StepsBand from '../../../components/pages/partners/StepsBand.astro';
import Reinforcement from '../../../components/pages/partners/Reinforcement.astro';
import PageEnhancements from '../../../components/pages/partners/PageEnhancements.astro';
import { HOURS, LINKS, TRACKING_MONTHS, meta } from '../../../components/pages/partners/partners';
import { C3_TRANSITION, CAMPUS_INCLUDES, CAMPUS_STEPS, DELIVERY_MODEL, EMPATHY, HEADLINE, METHOD, MICRO_COMMITMENT, POSITIONING, PROGRAM_SCOPE_STATEMENT_EXAMS, READ_THE_EVIDENCE, SPEED_UNIVERSITIES, TRIAL_BAND_HEADING, TRIAL_LEAD, VALUE_PROPOSITION } from '../../../data/copy';
import { faqJsonLd } from '../../../lib/faq';
import { cta } from '../../../lib/mailto';
import { webPage } from '../../../lib/schema';

const PATH = '/partner-with-us/universities/';
// WP161-A (adversarial review A-02): the WebPage carries the page's own dateModified, its last visible change (it fell back to the build date). WP166-B: 2026-11-21 (the marketing review R3 changes).
const primary = cta('campus');

// WP155 (Opus Max run 2, kit 122, Polish 4): "Our Approach" no longer ends "in campus labs alongside academic studies"; the band's H2 ("Training Alongside the Degree") and its "In Parallel with the Degree" card state the timing, so the description below still rests on the body.
// WP54 (cycle-28 review, Kimi K4): the description states only what the page body states (the hero's "universities and colleges" and "Our Approach": "JobReady@Campus combines training, mentoring and placement support in campus labs alongside
// academic studies"). It carried the survey's 84.6% degree share ("Among surveyed completers, 84.6% hold a bachelor’s degree or higher."), a figure that is not on this page.
const { title, description } = meta(
  'JobReady@Campus for Universities and Colleges',
  'For universities and colleges: JobReady@Campus combines training, mentoring and placement support in campus labs, alongside academic studies.',
);

// Q8-route: the one-line cost answer with a link to the partner hub FAQ, which keeps the full answer (WP36).
// WP166-B (marketing review R3-14): "Does It Change Our Curriculum?" (Q16-curriculum) answers a dean's second question.
const FAQ_IDS = ['Q1-campus', 'Q10-campus', 'Q16-curriculum', 'Q8-route'];
// WP175 (C11, restored from dee46ac1^): the one line of "Start with One Campus" (WP57: no size cards; WP132: tracks and labs are agreed in co-design, as the closing band and What Happens Next say).
const START_LINE = 'Cohort size, tracks and labs are agreed in co-design.';
// WP175 (C8c): the gain creator, JobReady@Campus's vignette "Capacity Designed to Stay on Campus" word for word (doc 04 4.5: campus labs as blended-learning centers with facilitators trained by CodersTrust, PD-06, IN-09); no painId, so it relieves no ranked pain.
const gainCreator = { icon: 'landmark', title: 'Capacity Designed to Stay on Campus', text: 'Campus labs keep working as blended-learning centers, with CodersTrust-trained facilitators.', facts: ['IN-09', 'PD-06'] };
---

<LandingLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  path={PATH}
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Partner with Us', href: LINKS.hub }, { label: 'Universities' }]}
  jsonLd={[webPage({ path: PATH, name: title, description, dateModified: '2026-11-28' /* WP175 (owner decisions of 2026-11-28): the crafted C6 statement (Q5), and the CMF v3 bands (the transition line, the C5 empathy and method lines, the trial band, the gain creator and three steps, the short C10, the restored C11) */ }), faqJsonLd('universities', PATH, FAQ_IDS)]}
  stickyCta={{ label: primary.label, href: primary.href }}
>
  <!-- C1 · Identity hook -->
  <Tone cmf="C1">
    <HeroBand
      audience="For Universities and Colleges"
      title={HEADLINE.universities}
      lead={VALUE_PROPOSITION.universities}
      cta={{ label: primary.label, href: primary.href }}
      artSeed="partners-universities"
    />
  </Tone>
  <!-- GEO · What is CodersTrust? WP175: the "See the Program" link (WP20b) sits under the definition, so GEO directly follows the hero. -->
  <Tone cmf="GEO">
    <DefinitionBand />
    <RouteLink kicker="See the Program" label="See Campus Delivery Details" href={LINKS.campus} />
  </Tone>

  <!-- C2–C4, declared compressed (WP47, owner decision 2026-10-15, recast 2026-11-28). WP34 (cycle-11 review): the Bangladesh graduate-unemployment tile (PX-03) is gone from this global page; the employer-skills tile (PX-05) stays.
       The PX-02 and PX-05 tiles are pains P1 and P2 (doc 04 4.5), the card below is P3, and the band ends with the C3 transition line. -->
  <Tone cmf="C2-C4 (compressed)">
    <ProblemBand
      title="Degrees Alone Are Not Turning into Jobs"
      bluf="Capable students finish their degrees, and employers still say they cannot find the skills they need."
      factIds={['PX-02', 'PX-05']}
      transition={C3_TRANSITION}
    >
      <!-- WP166-B (marketing review R3-40): the students' pain is the 19M+ tile (PX-02, as on Home and YouthWIDE) in place of the card "Degree holders struggle to find work" ("A degree alone does not guarantee a job offer."). -->
      <GainsPains
        slot="lead"
        pains={[
          // WP46 (cycle-22 review): the employers' pain is the 72% tile directly below (PX-05, worldwide), so a card that restated it is gone; the two pains left are the students' and the institution's.
          // WP38 (cycle-15 review): a general institutional pain, stated in one line like its neighbor; it rests on no CodersTrust fact.
          // WP49 (cycle-24 review): the line says what the institution needs ("is rarely collected" was a claim about the whole sector).
          // WP51 (cycle-26 review): the pain is headed as the goal ("Build Placement Results You Can Publish"); it was "Institutions Lack Placement Results They Can Publish", which presumed the reader's institution is deficient. The line under it is unchanged.
          // WP58 (cycle-30 review, GLM L4): the pain is stated as a pain, "Placement Results Are Hard to Publish" (the goal-framed "Build Placement Results You Can Publish" sat inside a list of pains). The line under it is unchanged.
          // WP175: it is P3 (data-pain), the pain the third campus card relieves.
          { id: 'P3', q: 'Placement results are hard to publish', text: 'Your institution needs placement data it can report to a board or ministry.' },
        ]}
      />
    </ProblemBand>
  </Tone>

  <!-- C5 · Guide: empathy → ORIGIN → authority → method (WP175, Q2 (a)).
       WP39 (cycle-16 review): no National University sentence here: the National University band (C7 below) states the relationship. WP66 (owner request 2026-10-20): the band's one proof line is the signed-agreement sentence for universities
       and colleges (SC-11b, `signed`). WP175: the TalentLEAP method line closes the band again (WP166-B R3-29 had moved it to How It Works). -->
  <Tone cmf="C5">
    <PartnerGuideBand
      empathy={EMPATHY.universities}
      signed="SC-11b"
      partnerGroup="academic"
      method={METHOD.universities}
      methodLast
    />
  </Tone>

  <!-- C6 · Mechanism (JobReady@Campus), the light variant of the mechanism band (WP175: the C7 trial band after it is the Klein one). WP166-B (marketing review R3-24): the approach closes with the page's one delivery-model sentence. -->
  <Tone cmf="C6">
    <HomeMechanism
      tone="airy"
      title="JobReady@Campus: Training Alongside the Degree"
      positioning={POSITIONING.universities}
      lead={DELIVERY_MODEL.text}
      blocks={[
        { label: 'Set Up', title: 'Campus Labs as Learning Centers', text: 'On-campus labs become blended-learning centers with facilitators trained by CodersTrust (Training of Trainers); faculty members act as coordinators.', icon: 'landmark' },
        { label: 'Prepare for Certification', title: 'Certification Preparation by Track', text: `${HOURS} training hours per certification, including exam preparation and one exam fee per trainee; exam eligibility and any further attempts are set per program.`, icon: 'award' },
        { label: 'Mentor and Place', title: 'Mentoring and Placement', text: `Three months of milestone-based mentoring and placement support, with outcome tracking for ${TRACKING_MONTHS} months after each course.`, icon: 'users' },
        { label: 'Alongside Studies', title: 'In Parallel with the Degree', text: 'Training runs in parallel with academic studies, with professional internships where employer placements are available.', icon: 'graduation-cap' },
      ]}
      link={{ label: 'About JobReady@Campus', href: LINKS.campus }}
    />
  </Tone>

  <!-- C7 · Proof (WP175, Q3 (a)): the trial band, led by the one-line trial lead, with the survey's employment readings in one sentence (compact); then the National University band, whose links go to the broader evidence (WP43:
       the band that WP38 put here said those links again), then Maria Dewan's story. Both stood before the problem band (WP24a). -->
  <Tone cmf="C7">
    <ProofBand title={TRIAL_BAND_HEADING} headlineFact="RC-01" trialLead={TRIAL_LEAD} statIds={[]} compact />
    <!-- WP166-B (marketing review R3-13): the heading states the claim (SC-04, SC-05; it said "The National University Partnership"), and the qualifier is the note under the two cards (it was the lead above them). -->
    <PairedEvidence
      eyebrow="Our Partnerships"
      title="Official Training Partner of the World’s Second-Largest University by Enrollment"
      note="These cards describe the learners being onboarded and National University’s size, not learners trained by CodersTrust."
      noteFacts={['SC-04', 'SC-05']}
      items={[
        { id: 'SC-04', label: 'Official Training Partner', drop: ' (the university’s own learners, not learners trained by CodersTrust)' },
        { id: 'SC-05', label: 'National University' },
      ]}
    />
    <LearnerVoice story="maria-dewan" excerpt="Maria Dewan was a third-year Biology student when she first came across Her Power, where CodersTrust was a training partner." program="Her Power" tone="white" />
  </Tone>

  <!-- C8 · Features to benefits. WP39 (cycle-16 review): three short cards in place of the concern / inclusion / benefit matrix, in the order of the three pains in C2 (the PX-02 and PX-05 tiles, then "Placement Results Are Hard to Publish").
       WP175: the cards are CAMPUS_INCLUDES (the same words, with painId P1 to P3), then the gain creator and "How It Works in Three Steps" (CAMPUS_STEPS). -->
  <Tone cmf="C8">
    <IncludesBand
      title="What Your Students and Your Institution Get"
      cards={[...CAMPUS_INCLUDES, gainCreator]}
      scope={PROGRAM_SCOPE_STATEMENT_EXAMS}
    />
    <HowItWorks steps={CAMPUS_STEPS} />
  </Tone>

  <!-- C9 · Objections, then the due-diligence view (WP34, cycle-11 review: one item and a link stand in for the four diligence cards) -->
  <Tone cmf="C9">
    <FAQBand
      audience="universities"
      ids={FAQ_IDS}
      title="Questions Universities Ask"
    />
    <DueDiligenceView brief id="due-diligence" />
  </Tone>

  <!-- C10 · Differentiation (WP175): the short band, USPs 3 and 4 (doc 04 4.5); the full comparison table stays off this page (WP30c, WP47). -->
  <Tone cmf="C10">
    <DifferenceBand usps={['credential', 'infrastructure']} />
  </Tone>

  <!-- C11 · Offer (WP175, restored from dee46ac1^). WP57 (cycle-29 review, Grok R5): no size cards, so no pilot size is recommended to a campus; the band is its heading and one line (OfferCards with no cards), and it holds no button of its own.
       WP133 (Opus High run 8): one path, so the heading names it. -->
  <Tone cmf="C11">
    <OfferCards eyebrow="" title="Start with One Campus" lead={START_LINE} cards={[]} />
  </Tone>

  <!-- C12 · Risk reversal (immediately before C13). WP175: the first point is the dee46ac1^ line again, now that C11 states the start line. -->
  <Tone cmf="C12">
    <RiskReversalBand
      title="Start with a Pilot, Then Decide on Evidence"
      points={[
        { icon: 'rocket', title: 'A Pilot Comes First', text: 'Start with a first campus program and see its results.' },
        { icon: 'target', title: 'Scorecard Thresholds', text: 'Thresholds are agreed before the first cohort; a missed threshold triggers a corrective plan.' },
        { icon: 'handshake', title: 'Expansion Is Your Decision', text: 'You decide whether to add campuses or tracks after the pilot.' },
        { icon: 'shield', title: 'Independent Evaluation Welcome', text: 'We support third-party evaluation of outcomes.' },
      ]}
    />
  </Tone>

  <!-- C13 · Call to action. WP166-B (marketing review R3-39): the reassurance line the other route pages carry ("A discovery session is a conversation, not a commitment."). -->
  <Tone cmf="C13">
    <CTABand
      id="cta"
      heading="Let’s Bring JobReady@Campus to Your Students"
      cta={{ label: primary.label, href: primary.href }}
      secondary={{ label: READ_THE_EVIDENCE, href: LINKS.evidence }}
      urgency={SPEED_UNIVERSITIES.text}
      micro={MICRO_COMMITMENT}
    />
  </Tone>

  <!-- C14 · Next steps -->
  <Tone cmf="C14">
    <StepsBand
      steps={[
        { title: 'Discovery Session', text: 'A conversation about your students, programs and timeline.' },
        { title: 'Co-Design', text: 'Tracks, campus labs and the pilot scorecard are shaped with you.' },
        { title: 'Agreement', text: 'Scope, schedule and the pilot scorecard are agreed.' },
        { title: 'First cohort in training', text: 'CodersTrust-trained facilitators begin the first cohort in your labs.' },
      ]}
    />
    <Reinforcement logos={false} reminder={false} />
  </Tone>

  <PageEnhancements />
</LandingLayout>

